nion","ingredient/onion"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Fish","ingredient/fish"],["Puff pastry","ingredient/puff-pastry"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Wine","ingredient/wine"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Custard","ingredient/custard"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Lobster meat","ingredient/lobster-meat"],["White wine","ingredient/white-wine"],["Wheat","ingredient/wheat"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."}],"cont":"Oceanic cuisine","img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/6/6a/Jacques_Lameloise%2C_escab%C3%A8che_d%27%C3%A9crevisses_sur_gaspacho_d%27asperge_et_cresson.jpg/500px-Jacques_Lameloise%2C_escab%C3%A8che_d%27%C3%A9crevisses_sur_gaspacho_d%27asperge_et_cresson.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Jacques Lameloise - Editer par Arnaud 25","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jacques_Lameloise%2C_escab%C3%A8che_d'%C3%A9crevisses_sur_gaspacho_d'asperge_et_cresson.jpg"}},"cuisine/marshallese-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/marshallese-cuisine","n":"Marshallese cuisine","c":"#55b8ad","crumb":[["Oceania","cuisines#oceania"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Marshall Is.","intro":[["Marshallese cuisine comprises the fare, foods, beverages and foodways of the Marshall Islands, including its food-related customs and traditions. Common indigenous and traditional foods include breadfruit, coconut, bananas, papaya, seafood, pandanus and bwiro (fermented breadfruit and coconut milk). Additional imported foods, such as rice and flour, are also a part of people's diets and contribute to the cuisine as well. The practice of food preservation is a part of the history of the islands, and continues to occur today."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"marshallese-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marshallese_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"School and Community Garden Cookbook (TerraCircle)","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"terracircle.org.au","note":"2025 Marshall Islands recipe book from the Canvasback Wellness Centre in Majuro, with a downloadable PDF.","url":"https://terracircle.org.au/?p=4913","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]}],"cont":"Oceanic cuisine","img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/f/f6/Marshall_Islands_PICT0650_%284776527309%29.jpg/500px-Marshall_Islands_PICT0650_%284776527309%29.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Christopher Johnson from Tokyo, Japan","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marshall_Islands_PICT0650_(4776527309).jpg"}},"ingredient/milk":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/milk","n":"Milk","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 70 dishes across 60 cuisines","intro":[["Milk is usually a white liquid food (but can be shades of yellow, cream, pink, or brown) produced by the mammary glands of lactating mammals. It is the primary source of nutrition for young mammals before they are able to digest solid food. Milk contains many nutrients, including calcium and protein, as well as lactose and saturated fat; the enzyme lactase is needed to break down lactose. Immune factors and immune-modulating components in milk contribute to milk immunity. The first milk, which is called colostrum, contains antibodies and immune-modulating components that strengthen the immune system against many diseases."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-milk"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milk"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":60,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"