duced is often carbon dioxide, or occasionally hydrogen."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-leavening-agent"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leavening_agent"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Digestive biscuit","dish/digestive-biscuit"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Malic acid","ingredient/malic-acid"],["Malt extract","ingredient/malt-extract"],["Sodium bicarbonate","ingredient/sodium-bicarbonate"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Tartaric acid","ingredient/tartaric-acid"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Wholemeal","ingredient/wholemeal"]]}]},"ingredient/small-intestine":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/small-intestine","n":"Small intestine","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The small intestine or small bowel is an organ in the gastrointestinal tract where most of the absorption of nutrients from food takes place. It lies between the stomach and large intestine, and receives bile and pancreatic juice through the pancreatic duct to aid in digestion. The small intestine is about 6.5 metres (21 feet) long and folds many times to fit in the abdomen. Although it is longer than the large intestine, it is called the small intestine because it is narrower in diameter."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-small-intestine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Small_intestine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine",[["Gopchang","dish/gopchang"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Big intestine","ingredient/big-intestine"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"]]}]},"dish/hedgehog-slice":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/hedgehog-slice","n":"Hedgehog slice","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Hedgehog slice is an uncooked flat, square or bar-shaped chocolate snack, similar to rocky road, made of chocolate and crushed or complete biscuits, or rice puffs. Nuts may also be added. It usually has a topping of chocolate icing, upon which may be sprinkled coconut, hundreds and thousands, or other kinds of sprinkles or raisins (e.g. chocolate or coffee flavoured, etc.)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-hedgehog-slice"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hedgehog_slice"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"],["Thuringian cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine-thuringia"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Biscuit","ingredient/biscuit"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Chocolate","ingredient/chocolate"],["Cookie","ingredient/cookie"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Quick German Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"quick-german-recipes.com","note":"Long-running site by German-born cook Gerhild Fulson (Oma) with traditional German home recipes.","url":"https://www.quick-german-recipes.com/about-me.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Dirndl Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dirndlkitchen.com","note":"Blog of German and Bavarian recipes, from main dishes to holiday baking.","url":"https://dirndlkitchen.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Quick German Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"quick-german-recipes.com","note":"Thuringia page on German-born cook Gerhild Fulson's long-running German recipe site.","url":"https://www.quick-german-recipes.com/thuringia.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from German cuisine","links":[["Baumkuchen","dish/baumkuchen"],["Bockwurst","dish/bockwurst"],["Buchteln","dish/buchteln"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chrain","dish/chrain"],["Dampfnudel","dish/dampfnudel"],["Eel 