method of preparing red meat, white meat, and seafood which originated in the Paleolithic Era. Smoking adds flavor, improves the appearance of meat through the Maillard reaction, and when combined with curing it preserves the meat. When meat is cured then cold-smoked, the smoke adds phenols and other chemicals that have an antimicrobial effect on the meat. Hot smoking has less impact on preservation and is primarily used for taste and to slow-cook the meat. Interest in barbecue and smoking is on the rise worldwide."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-smoked-meat"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoked_meat"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Serbian cuisine","cuisine/serbian-cuisine",[["Pasulj","dish/pasulj"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Apium graveolens var. dulce","ingredient/apium-graveolens-var-dulce"],["Bean","ingredient/bean"],["Bell pepper","ingredient/bell-pepper"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["White bean","ingredient/white-bean"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/7/72/O_Piornedo%2C_Don%C3%ADs%2C_Cervantes_10.jpg/500px-O_Piornedo%2C_Don%C3%ADs%2C_Cervantes_10.jpg","w":500,"h":334,"by":"Ramon Piñeiro","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:O_Piornedo%2C_Don%C3%ADs%2C_Cervantes_10.jpg"}},"dish/stromboli-food":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/stromboli-food","n":"Stromboli (food)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian-American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Stromboli are a type of baked bread filled with various Italian cheeses (typically mozzarella) and Italian cold cuts (typically salami, capocollo, and bresaola) or vegetables, and marinara sauce, served hot. The dough is either Italian bread dough or pizza dough. Stromboli are an Italian-American dish invented in Philadelphia by the mid-20th century. The dish is ultimately named for the volcanic island off the coast of Sicily, by way of the 1950 Roberto Rossellini film of the same name."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-stromboli-food"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stromboli_(food)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian-American cuisine","cuisine/italian-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"]]},{"h":"More from Italian-American cuisine","links":[["Chicken Francese","dish/chicken-francese"],["Fettuccine Alfredo","dish/fettuccine-alfredo"],["Garlic bread","dish/garlic-bread"],["Italian beef","dish/italian-beef"],["Italian tomato pie","dish/italian-tomato-pie"],["Rollatini","dish/rollatini"],["Spaghetti and meatballs","dish/spaghetti-and-meatballs"],["Tetrazzini","dish/tetrazzini"],["Vodka sauce","dish/vodka-sauce"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/f/f1/HomemadeStromboliAug05.jpg/500px-HomemadeStromboliAug05.jpg","w":500,"h":555,"by":"Jeremy Noble at https://www.flickr.com/photos/uberculture/","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HomemadeStromboliAug05.jpg"}},"ingredient/latundan-banana":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/latundan-banana","n":"Latundan banana","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["The Latundan banana (also called Tundan, silk banana, Pisang raja sereh, Manzana (or Manzano) banana, or apple banana) is a triploid hybrid banana cultivar of the AAB group from the Philippines. It is one of the most common banana cultivars in Southeast Asia, along with Lakatan and Saba bananas. Its Malaysian name is pisang rastali."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-latundan-banana"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latundan_banana"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Ace